    "done_when": "Using the same run population and death classification that docs/research/scripts/scan_local_lane_deaths.py produces (import it, do not re-derive it), compare the review/high and review/xhigh attempts on each candidate confounder: dispatch date and hour, project, the reviewed node's diff size and the reviewed run's own prompt size, whether the review was of a repair, a re-review or an original run, lane load at dispatch where the lane document history records it, wall time and turn count at death, and backend and model. For each confounder state whether the high cell is drawn from a different range than the xhigh cell, and restrict the xhigh cell to the high cell's range on every confounder that differs, reporting the restricted death rate with its count. A report at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s22-coord/review-effort-confounders/report.md states the result in one of three words (effort, confounded, inconclusive) with the counts behind it, names the population a re-dispatch experiment should draw from and the smallest sample that would separate the two rates, and embeds one figure saved beside it: death rate by effort with the restricted xhigh rate, no gridlines, top and right spines removed, each series labelled directly. Nothing in the repository changes in this node. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete, printed and listed in artifacts. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Establish whether the death-rate gap between local-lane reviews at effort xhigh (392 dead of 1324 attempts) and at effort high (1 dead of 46), both recorded in docs/research/data/local-lane-deaths.json, survives the confounders that could produce it, so that the effort experiment the plan requires is designed against the right population.",
